rapikan bundles third-party data:

src/rapikan/data/roots.tsv
  Derived from hunspell-id, the Indonesian Hunspell dictionary distributed with
  LibreOffice (https://github.com/LibreOffice/dictionaries/tree/master/id,
  upstream https://github.com/shuLhan/hunspell-id), itself a continuation of
  "Kamus Indonesia" by Benitius Brevoort.
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0
  (src/rapikan/data/LICENSE-roots-LGPL-3.0.txt).
  Processing: word list and affix flags converted to root<TAB>allowed-affix-families
  by tools/build_roots.py. You may replace this file with your own version.

bench/ud_csui_stems.tsv
  Derived from UD_Indonesian-CSUI (Universal Dependencies,
  https://github.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_Indonesian-CSUI).
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0).
  Processing: word/lemma pairs extracted by tools/ud_to_gold.py; only affixed
  words with a single lemma kept. This file stays under CC BY-SA 4.0.

The downstream benchmark (bench/downstream.py) reads SmSA and EmoT (IndoNLU) and
NusaX-senti from their own repositories; none of that data is bundled.

All other files (code, slang.tsv, stopwords.txt, bench/gold_stems.tsv,
bench/heldout_stems.tsv) were written for rapikan and are MIT licensed.
